A||N||9||chester||Accel DFI or Haltec ECM - Does anyone have one?||||5||
Z||000000||chester||07-27-2001||08:49 AM||||I'm getting ready to get a programmable ECM for my GT.  I'm looking for some feedback from anyone that has either the Accel DFI or the Haltec ECM. Likes/dislikes, problems etc. I'm also looking for the pin out for the Accel unit so I can see what is involved it rewiring the engine harness. Any help is greatly appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||07-27-2001||10:12 AM||||I don't have the ones you list, but I do have an aftermarket system.<P>Electromotive TEC-II.  It is the best!  I separated all the wires on the harness, plugged them into the sensors and screwed the wires into the box.  It was tedious, but well worth it.  It's up to the user to figure out how to get the engine configured(read the manual 100 times and it isn't so hard).  It is amazing...while the engine is running, I can adjust certain parameters and hut ENTER and hear the engine run totally differnt!<BR>Mounting the trigger wheel is a pain though.<P>Absolutely NO hesitation.  <P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||07-27-2001||11:40 AM||||Joe, how much was your system?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||07-27-2001||12:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leadfoot:<BR><B>Joe, how much was your system?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It is about $1600.  Yes expensive, but it is more comprehensive than the others...does the accel even make it for 6cyl?  I think the $1600 includes the sensors too...I paid less because all my sensors were new off of the 3400.  2.8 sensors will work(all the GM values are the same).<P>You can program the system to react appropriately for add ons like turbos, superchargers, nitrous.  It has a General Purpose Output to control a solinoid too.<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000004||West Coast Fiero||07-27-2001||01:27 PM||||The Haltech E6GM V2 is currently in use on our turbocharged 3800 Series II. There have been no hiccups to date and it offers real time graphing and programing by use of a laptop or desk top computer. It gives you control of Every ( yes EVERY ), did I say every engine function. It is up to you whether it runs like crap, or the redline is set at 20,000 rpm, or compensate for 80 lbs of boost - it will let you put in anything, and it is made to operate with a stock 2.8 harness integrated with whatever engine you have - best part...$600, this includes warranty, technical support, and product upgrades.<P> visit <A HREF="http://www.haltech.com" TARGET=_blank>www.haltech.com</A> <P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fasterfiero||07-27-2001||07:25 PM||||I also have e6gm. If i were to do it over I would go with the speedpro/felpro unit. much better imo. much easier to program. in fact i think that the haltec is very difficult to program, and does not have the features that ease tuning. felpro/speedpro is about $2000.00. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||West Coast Fiero||07-27-2001||09:58 PM||||fasterfiero - do you have V1 or V2?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Terrybogin||07-27-2001||10:51 PM||||I have a very easily programmed, fast ECM. It has more adjustment than I know what to do with. It costed. . . $70. Tuning software about $100 and about $200 more for an eprom burner and eraser. It can run a DIS, distributer, TPI, TBI, 1 bar MAP, 2 bar MAP, speed density, mass air, function with a manual or automatic tranny, adjust TCC lockup, rev limiters, speed limiters, etc. . .  Don't overlook the OEM computers, they have a lot more going for them than you think. ||||reg||1
